    text The  argument is parsed and evaluated as a Python expression (technically speaking, an ) using the  and  mappings as global and local namespace. If the  dictionary is present and does not contain a value for the key , a reference to the dictionary of the built-in module  is inserted under that key before  is parsed. Overriding  can be used to restrict or change the available names, but this is  a security mechanism: the executed code can still access all builtins. If the  mapping is omitted it defaults to the  dictionary. If both mappings are omitted, the source is executed with the  and  in the environment where  is called. Note,  will only have access to the  (non-locals) in the enclosing environment if they are already referenced in the scope that is calling  (e.g. via a  statement).
