      text class
      text float
      text (
      text string
      text /
      text )
    text Return a floating-point number constructed from a number or a string.
    text Examples:
    text >>> float('+1.23') 1.23 >>> float(' -12345\n') -12345.0 >>> float('1e-003') 0.001 >>> float('+1E6') 1000000.0 >>> float('-Infinity') -inf
    text If the argument is a string, it should contain a decimal number, optionally preceded by a sign, and optionally embedded in whitespace. The optional sign may be  or ; a  sign has no effect on the value produced. The argument may also be a string representing a NaN (not-a-number), or positive or negative infinity. More precisely, the input must conform to the  production rule in the following grammar, after leading and trailing whitespace characters are removed:
    text '+'
    text '-'
    text '+'
    link floatvalue #grammar-token-float-floatvalue
    text :  |  :  |  :  : <a Unicode decimal digit, i.e. characters in Unicode general category Nd> :  ([] )* : []   |  [] : ( | ) []  :  [] :  |  |  : []
    card
