    text If you want to convert an integer number to an octal string either with the prefix “0o” or not, you can use either of the following ways.
    text >>> '%#o' % 10, '%o' % 10 ('0o12', '12') >>> format(10, '#o'), format(10, 'o') ('0o12', '12') >>> f'{10:#o}', f'{10:o}' ('0o12', '12')
