    text buffering
    text Binary files are buffered in fixed-size chunks; the size of the buffer is max(min(blocksize, 8 MiB), DEFAULT_BUFFER_SIZE) when the device block size is available. On most systems, the buffer will typically be 128 kilobytes long.
    text “Interactive” text files (files for which  returns ) use line buffering. Other text files use the policy described above for binary files.
