    text Return a new sorted list from the items in iterable.
    text Has two optional arguments which must be specified as keyword arguments.
    text key specifies a function of one argument that is used to extract a comparison key from each element in iterable (for example, key=str.lower). The default value is None (compare the elements directly).
    text reverse is a boolean value. If set to True, then the list elements are sorted as if each comparison were reversed.
    text Use  to convert an old-style  function to a  function.
