    text super()[name]
    text Also note that, aside from the zero argument form,  is not limited to use inside methods. The two argument form specifies the arguments exactly and makes the appropriate references. The zero argument form only works inside a class definition, as the compiler fills in the necessary details to correctly retrieve the class being defined, as well as accessing the current instance for ordinary methods.
    link super() #super
    text For practical suggestions on how to design cooperative classes using , see .
